{
  "_about": "Status tags and rules. popup: false = no text pops up when it lands (its icon and body effect already show it; only big moments like stun/freeze/fear/taunt/silence pop text). dot: damage over time, every application adds a STACK (no limit, each stack has its own timer, all stacks of one kind tick together every tickMs). control: bosses take it for half as long (statusDurationScale). Numbers here are defaults a skill/item spec can override. stacking: like dot it stacks (each stack own timer) but deals no damage (chill). instant: no lasting status (knockback). Stat debuffs (weaken, armorBreak, curse, blind, mark) refresh per source; different sources add up. shield: absorbs damage (amount / percentMaxHp / attackMultiplier), lasts durationMs or until broken, optional onBreak {damageMultiplier, damageType}; invulnerable: takes no damage at all, optional healPercentOnEnd. debuff: true marks harmful statuses (Rally Cry's cleanse removes one kind of them). parry: hits against the holder are stopped completely (Samurai's Focus Stance). guaranteedCrit: the holder's next basic attack is a sure crit, then it is used up. typeBonus: false = the caster's +% damage-type items do NOT boost this DoT (Poison: Shadow Charm only boosts dark hits). regenBoost: heals percentMaxHpPerSec of max health every second for its duration (Bard's Ballad of Rest).",
